The historical fix (ClickHouse PR #39560, "Fix typo and extra dots in exception messages from OverCommitTracker"):

```cpp
return "Memory overcommit isn't used: OvercommitTracker isn't set";
...
return "Memory overcommit isn't used: Waiting time or overcommit denominator are set to zero";
...
return "Query was selected to stop by OvercommitTracker";
...
return "Waiting timeout for memory to be freed is reached";
...
return "Memory overcommit has freed not enough memory";
```

I believe the actual diff removed the trailing dots and changed ". " to ": " in first two, fixed "orvercommit" → "overcommit". Let me make this edit, then commit. This file (MemoryTracker.cpp) might be touched by other agents — use flock for edit+commit to be safe. Actually requirement 4 says wrap edit + stage/commit in one flock for shared files. MemoryTracker.cpp is plausible shared. I'll script it with python inside flock.

Actually simpler: do the Edit now, then commit with flock. But concurrent agents could edit the same file between my edit and commit — their uncommitted changes would be staged by my `git add` if I add the whole file. To be safe, use flock covering edit + add + commit.

Let me write a script.

args.command:
cd /workspace && flock /tmp/ch_git.lock bash -c '
python3 - <<"EOF"
p = "src/Common/MemoryTracker.cpp"
s = open(p).read()
old = """    case OvercommitResult::NONE:
        return "Memory overcommit isn\x27t used. OvercommitTracker isn\x27t set.";
    case OvercommitResult::DISABLED:
        return "Memory overcommit isn\x27t used. Waiting time or orvercommit denominator are set to zero.";
    case OvercommitResult::MEMORY_FREED:
        throw DB::Exception(DB::ErrorCodes::LOGICAL_ERROR, "OvercommitResult::MEMORY_FREED shouldn\x27t be asked for description");
    case OvercommitResult::SELECTED:
        return "Query was selected to stop by OvercommitTracker.";
    case OvercommitResult::TIMEOUTED:
        return "Waiting timeout for memory to be freed is reached.";
    case OvercommitResult::NOT_ENOUGH_FREED:
        return "Memory overcommit has freed not enough memory.";
"""
new = """    case OvercommitResult::NONE:
        return "Memory overcommit isn\x27t used: OvercommitTracker isn\x27t set";
    case OvercommitResult::DISABLED:
        return "Memory overcommit isn\x27t used: Waiting time or overcommit denominator are set to zero";
    case OvercommitResult::MEMORY_FREED:
        throw DB::Exception(DB::ErrorCodes::LOGICAL_ERROR, "OvercommitResult::MEMORY_FREED shouldn\x27t be asked for description");
    case OvercommitResult::SELECTED:
        return "Query was selected to stop by OvercommitTracker";
    case OvercommitResult::TIMEOUTED:
        return "Waiting timeout for memory to be freed is reached";
    case OvercommitResult::NOT_ENOUGH_FREED:
        return "Memory overcommit has freed not enough memory";
"""
assert old in s, "pattern not found"
open(p, "w").write(s.replace(old, new))
EOF
git add src/Common/MemoryTracker.cpp && mkdir -p requirement_patches && git diff --cached > requirement_patches/overcommittracker-message-cleanup.diff && git commit -q -m "impl: overcommittracker-message-cleanup"
' && wc -c requirement_patches/overcommittracker-message-cleanup.diff

